  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forests for Sustainable Development (FSD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FSD programme goal is to improve conservation of natural forest resources, biodiversity, and ecosystem services and increase livelihoods opportunities and household incomes in the Bale eco-region and Guji-Borena landscape.
It targets 20 woredas, 142 kebeles, 50,550 households under Participatory Forest Management, 2150 youth (215 groups), and women. Estimated GHG reductions 20,485536.59 tonnes in CO2 equivalent.</narrative>
  </description>
